olve within 24 hours) or erythema multiforme (which typically shows target lesions and is often associated with systemic triggers). The model prediction of 22.54% for urticaria pigmentosa is supported by the visual findings, which align with the clinical presentation of this condition. Although no precedent cases were found, the visual and guideline-based analysis strongly supports urticaria pigmentosa as the most likely diagnosis.'}
