[Handbook: erythema annulare centrifigum]
This curious, but uncommon, condition is thought to be a ‘hypersensitivity reaction’ perhaps to drugs or infection, but, in most cases, a trigger is not identified. Small dermal blood vessels are cuffed by clusters of lymphocytes. Erythema annulare centrifugum (EAC) is commoner in adults than children. Do not confuse this with the other erythemas (see Box 11.6).  This curious, but uncommon, condition is thought to be a ‘hypersensitivity reaction’ perhaps to drugs or infection, but, in most cases, a trigger is not identified. Small dermal blood vessels are cuffed by clusters of lymphocytes. Erythema annulare centrifugum (EAC) is commoner in adults than children. Do not confuse this with the other erythemas (see Box 11.6).
The greasy,ill-defined erythematous papular rash involves the central face but is not oedematous and spares the eyelids. The scalp may be erythematous and scaly, but hair is not usually affected. Seborrhoeic dermatitis may also involve the central chest, central back, and flexures.  The greasy,ill-defined erythematous papular rash involves the central face but is not oedematous and spares the eyelids. The scalp may be erythematous and scaly, but hair is not usually affected. Seborrhoeic dermatitis may also involve the central chest, central back, and flexures.


