Synonyms: chigoe flea, sand flea, chigger, jigger.  Synonyms: chigoe flea, sand flea, chigger, jigger.  Infestation with a flea (1mm long) endemic in Central America, the Caribbean, and sub-Saharan Africa causes tungiasis. The flea resides in warm, dry soil/sandy beaches. Usual hosts——pigs, cats, rodents. The $mathcal{G}$ burrows into the skin, feeding from dermal capillaries, enlarging, and breathing through a cutaneous punctum. After 2 days to 3 weeks, $150-$ 200 eggs/day are released from the punctum. The flea dies in situ after 3-4 weeks and is eventually shed in a crust.  Infestation with a flea (1mm long) endemic in Central America, the Caribbean, and sub-Saharan Africa causes tungiasis. The flea resides in warm, dry soil/sandy beaches. Usual hosts——pigs, cats, rodents. The $\mathcal{G}$ burrows into the skin, feeding from dermal capillaries, enlarging, and breathing through a cutaneous punctum. After 2 days to 3 weeks, $150-$ 200 eggs/day are released from the punctum. The flea dies in situ after 3-4 weeks and is eventually shed in a crust.  What should I look for?  What should I look for?  •    History of travel to an endemic area. •    History of travel to an endemic area. What should I do?  What should I do?  •    Extract surgically after local anaesthetic (see Fig. 8.6b). •    Extract surgically after local anaesthetic (see Fig. 8.6b).

