· Acrodermatitis continua/acrodermatitis of Hallopeau: affects one or more digits. Sterile pustules form beneath and around the nail plate, which is lifted off by crust and lakes of pus. Nail loss may be permanent and associated with resorptive osteolysis. Very potent topical steroids or oral retinoids are indicated. Parakeratosis pustulosa: affects a single digit in young children—-the skin is erythematous and scaly. Pustules/vesicles may be present early but do not persist, and changes look eczematous. The nail plate lifts up and becomes thickened. The condition is chronic but self-limiting. Topical steroids may be helpful. It is uncertain whether this condition is a form of eczema or psoriasis.  · Acrodermatitis continua/acrodermatitis of Hallopeau: affects one or more digits. Sterile pustules form beneath and around the nail plate, which is lifted off by crust and lakes of pus. Nail loss may be permanent and associated with resorptive osteolysis. Very potent topical steroids or oral retinoids are indicated. Parakeratosis pustulosa: affects a single digit in young children—-the skin is erythematous and scaly. Pustules/vesicles may be present early but do not persist, and changes look eczematous. The nail plate lifts up and becomes thickened. The condition is chronic but self-limiting. Topical steroids may be helpful. It is uncertain whether this condition is a form of eczema or psoriasis.

